hat":"provisional NO, but no job found a whole-order-end candidate"}],"schema":"eo-case-bundle/v1","status":"no","text_pointers":[{"first_1500_characters":"Instrument: EO:10510\nSource: https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1953-12-19/pdf/FR-1953-12-19.pdf\nSHA-256 of the downloaded file: 6bfd0907095cf35b2591b2131b91bf74b840cb527d8917119ef75b3c80a94267\nLocation: 18 FR 8527, PDF pages 1-3 (confidence high)\nMachine-extracted text layer of the official PDF (OCR for 1936-1994 scans). May contain recognition errors and parts of neighbouring documents on the same pages. Not an authenticated transcription: check the PDF pages.\n\n=== PDF page 1 of 80 ===\nÆ \\\nV\nREGISTER\nVOLUME 18 ' S * ,  1934\n*  (J N i T t O ^\nNUMBER 247\nWashington, Saturday, December 19, 1953\nTITLE 3— THE PRESIDENT\nEXECUTIVE ORDER 10510\nEstablishing  a S e a l f o r t h e D e p a r t m e n t\nof H ealth , E d u c a t io n, a n d W e l f a r e\nWHEREAS the Secretary of Health,  \nEducation, and W elfare has adopted and  \nhas recommended that I  approve a seal  \nof office for the Department of Health,  \nEducation, and Welfare, the design of  \nwhich accompanies and is hereby made a  \npart of this order, and which is described  \nin heraldic terms as follows:\nSHIELD: Argent an open book w ith san­\nguine binding charged overall with a staff  \nof Aesculapius paleways w ithin an annulet  \nof chain all proper.\nCREST: On a wreath argent and sanguine  \nan American bald eagle displayed and wings  \npartially inverted proper.\nBelow the shield a white scroll inscribed with  \nthe motto “SPES ANCH O R A VIT A E ” in black \nletters, all on a circular sanguine background  \nwithin a white band","path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/texts/EO_10510.txt","sha256":"ed1a2c28a7b327879264b458fcef470f45986a89075c37db1d60e04552ae30de","source":{"line":783,"path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"0aa5cdc445e8583d3d2ad36d4cbbaff16e91e83f2798ad9f7550d0970a791c3c"}}]}
